{"id": "EUVD-2026-80561", "enisaUuid": "dde38da9-e47f-3cd6-85d7-9cb0fdab222b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npowerpc/mm: fix wrong addr_pfn tracking in compound vmemmap population\n\nvmemmap_populate_compound_pages() uses addr_pfn to determine the PFN\noffset within a compound page and to decide whether the current vmemmap\nslot should be populated as a head page mapping or should reuse a tail\npage mapping.\n\nHowever, addr_pfn is advanced manually in parallel with addr.  The loop\nitself progresses in vmemmap address space, so each PAGE_SIZE step in addr\ncovers PAGE_SIZE / sizeof(struct page) struct page slots.  Since addr_pfn\nis compared against nr_pages in data-PFN units, it should advance by the\nsame number of PFNs.  The existing manual increments do not match that and\ntherefore do not reliably track the PFN corresponding to the current addr.\n\nAs a result, pfn_offset can be computed from the wrong PFN and the code\ncan make the head/tail decision for the wrong compound-page position.\n\nFix this by deriving addr_pfn directly from the current vmemmap address\ninstead of carrying it as loop state.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:32:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:55:35", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b96be860673f9fbbf12cdadb0b25fc4d6d4d207f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e163c7184acf36ac20a248498f4a16016057ca01", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9c914b7a0bd18834505c65f22225ce22c152b2d9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7968852a7ca3ce81477ec5b4494a28d612f35a97", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/89a4ae32764172468dea303eb6ae90fe6c859712"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89961", "GHSA-25fw-r826-pmc4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0790ae62-9b1c-34f3-894c-fc7558a6692a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "411f0641-ad48-3d8b-bf3a-848444c9d3b5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2b79c0d79683d552369bb9a7282c1f0226fc566 <7968852a7ca3ce81477ec5b4494a28d612f35a97"}, {"id": "5b8dd797-e2f6-32e7-a127-c16988d2f85f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8f4dc1f3-bb7d-3a10-97e0-18fdea1ff372", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "9eaf2aa2-ddf6-3bf3-9a3b-10260c474fb9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2b79c0d79683d552369bb9a7282c1f0226fc566 <e163c7184acf36ac20a248498f4a16016057ca01"}, {"id": "afdd0951-65a9-3a7a-ad63-43cf02aca498", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2b79c0d79683d552369bb9a7282c1f0226fc566 <9c914b7a0bd18834505c65f22225ce22c152b2d9"}, {"id": "c1c8fecf-f9f2-341d-9950-87d2700087e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "c53e028c-ab64-3325-8ece-744699d00a05", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2b79c0d79683d552369bb9a7282c1f0226fc566 <89a4ae32764172468dea303eb6ae90fe6c859712"}, {"id": "d8e0e99f-cd33-3d28-bfc7-a405dbfd6116", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "d93bcb7c-b365-3152-becb-4cb58fc759e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "dde6012c-dfa3-3243-964c-5123a934bf8e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.5"}, {"id": "e8a4077a-8ae5-3033-af2a-45ab793d95d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f2b79c0d79683d552369bb9a7282c1f0226fc566 <b96be860673f9fbbf12cdadb0b25fc4d6d4d207f"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2c201f91-66d4-37f0-8f33-6ff91b29f1ce", "vendor": {